meta {
  name: Update Step - Incident Type
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

put {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngPersonId/incidents/:id/steps/incident-type
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  youngPersonId: 1
  id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "incident_types": [
      1,
      2,
      3
    ],
    "other_incident_type": null
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Step: Type of Incident
  
  This endpoint updates the second step - selecting incident types from checkboxes.
  
  ## Request Body:
  - `incident_types`: Array of incident type IDs (from master data) or type names
  - `other_incident_type`: Optional text description if "other" type is selected
  
  ## How it works:
  1. Fetch available incident types from GET `/incidents/master-data/incident-types` endpoint
  2. The master data returns incident type records with `id`, `incident_type`, `house_id`, `client_id`
  3. Send an array of incident type IDs to associate with this incident
  4. Alternatively, you can send type names (strings) and they will be created if they don't exist
  5. Uses many-to-many relationship (pivot table) - old associations are replaced with new ones
  
  ## Example with IDs (recommended):
  ```json
  {
    "incident_types": [1, 2, 3],
    "other_incident_type": null
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example with names (creates if not exists):
  ```json
  {
    "incident_types": [
      "physical_assault",
      "verbal_threats_abuse"
    ],
    "other_incident_type": "Custom incident type description"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response:
  Returns the updated incident record with the `types` relationship loaded showing all associated incident types.
}
